<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">1947</h1><p class="ref-lede">1947 in world history: 47 events, 12 births, 30 deaths, 8 works, 8 states founded and 13 that came to an end. 688 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/1943">1943</a><a href="/years/1944">1944</a><a href="/years/1945">1945</a><a href="/years/1946">1946</a><a href="/years/1947" aria-current="page">1947</a><a href="/years/1948">1948</a><a href="/years/1949">1949</a><a href="/years/1950">1950</a><a href="/years/1951">1951</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-1">1 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">American and British zones of Germany merge into the Bizone</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> combined the economic administration of their occupation zones in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. The Bizone, joined by the French zone in 1949, became the nucleus of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-germany">West Germany</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-3">3 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">US Congress proceedings are televised for the first time</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The opening session of the 80th Congress was broadcast on television, a first for the American legislature. Regular television coverage of both chambers followed only decades later.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/chiang-kai-shek" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chiang-kai-shek.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-28">28 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">An uprising in Taiwan is violently put down by the Nationalist government</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">An uprising in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a> against the Kuomintang-led government of the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> was crushed under governor Chen Yi and president <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chiang-kai-shek">Chiang Kai-shek</a>; an estimated 18,000 to 28,000 civilians died. It was a critical impetus for the Taiwan independence movement.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/republic-of-china">Republic of China</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuomintang">Kuomintang</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chiang-kai-shek">Chiang Kai-shek</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-1">1 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">International Monetary Fund begins operations</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Created at the Bretton Woods conference of 1944, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/international-monetary-fund">IMF</a> opened for business in Washington. It was designed to stabilise exchange rates and lend to countries in balance-of-payments difficulties.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/international-monetary-fund">International Monetary Fund</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-12">12 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Truman announces the Truman Doctrine</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Asking Congress for aid to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harry-s-truman">Harry Truman</a> pledged to support 'free peoples who are resisting attempted subjugation'. The doctrine framed US <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cold-war">Cold War</a> policy of containment.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-5">5 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">George Marshall proposes a plan to rebuild Europe</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">In a speech at Harvard, the US Secretary of State offered aid to European recovery. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marshall-plan">Marshall Plan</a> provided some $13 billion and deepened the divide between East and West.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-7">7 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Thor Heyerdahl's Kon-Tiki raft reaches Polynesia</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">After 101 days and some 7,000 km from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thor">Thor</a> Heyerdahl's balsa raft ran onto the reef at Raroia. The voyage showed that prehistoric people could have crossed the Pacific on such craft.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-15">15 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">India becomes independent as British rule ends</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">At midnight <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> became independent, a day after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>. Partition uprooted perhaps 15 million people and communal violence killed hundreds of thousands, possibly up to two million.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-14">14 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Chuck Yeager flies faster than sound</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Captain Chuck Yeager piloted the rocket-powered Bell X-1 past Mach 1 high over the Mojave Desert. It was the first confirmed supersonic flight in level flight, opening the age of supersonic aviation.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-25">25 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Hollywood studios blacklist the 'Hollywood Ten'</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Studio heads issued the Waldorf Statement, refusing to employ ten writers and directors cited for contempt of Congress. The Hollywood blacklist that followed ended or interrupted hundreds of careers.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-29">29 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The UN votes to partition Palestine</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The UN General Assembly adopted Resolution 181, recommending separate Jewish and Arab states with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> under international control. Fighting broke out the next day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-23">23 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Bell Labs demonstrates the transistor</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">John Bardeen and Walter Brattain showed colleagues at Bell Laboratories their point-contact <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transistor">transistor</a> amplifying a signal. Transistors replaced vacuum tubes and made modern electronics possible.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/indian-independence">Indian independence</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Indian independence refers to the end of British rule in India in 1947, when the subcontinent was partitioned into India and Pakistan.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/partition-of-india" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/partition-of-india.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/partition-of-india">Partition of India</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Partition of India was the division of British India into two independent dominions, India and Pakistan, on 14–15 August 1947.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/panglong-conference">Panglong Conference</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Panglong Conference was a meeting held at Panglong in the Shan States in February 1947, at which Aung San, representing the interim Burmese government, reached agreement with Shan, Kachin and Chin leaders.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/operation-bootstrap">Operation Bootstrap</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Operation Bootstrap was the programme launched in Puerto Rico in the late 1940s by Luis Muñoz Marín and Teodoro Moscoso to industrialise the island's farming economy.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/paris-peace-treaties-1947">Paris Peace Treaties (1947)</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Paris Peace Treaties were signed on 10 February 1947 between the Allied powers and the former Axis allies Italy, Romania, Hungary, Bulgaria and Finland.</p></div></li></ol></section>
