<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/british-empire"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/British%20Empire.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>British Empire</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">India gains independence, removing the empire's most vital possession</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/new-zealand"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/New%20Zealand.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>New Zealand</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Parliament adopts the Statute of Westminster, completing legislative independence</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/free-hanseatic-city-of-bremen"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Free%20Hanseatic%20City%20of%20Bremen.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Free Hanseatic City of Bremen</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Land of Bremen is re-established with Bremerhaven</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/british-raj"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/British%20Raj.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>British Raj</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Independence and partition create India and Pakistan on 14–15 August</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/myanmar"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Myanmar.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Myanmar</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Aung San and minority leaders agree to form a union at the Panglong Conference</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/language/hebrew"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Hebrew.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Hebrew</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The first Dead Sea Scrolls, including the oldest known manuscripts of the Hebrew Bible, are found near Qumran</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/indian-independence-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Indian%20independence%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Indian independence movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">British rule ends, and British India is partitioned into India and Pakistan</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/government/colonial-rule"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Colonial%20rule.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Colonial rule</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">British India becomes independent as India and Pakistan, amid the violence of partition</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/government/constitutional-monarchy"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Constitutional%20monarchy.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Constitutional monarchy</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Japan’s new constitution makes the emperor “the symbol of the State and of the unity of the people”</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/south-indian-megalithic-culture"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/South%20Indian%20megalithic%20culture.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>South Indian megalithic culture</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Mortimer Wheeler excavates Brahmagiri, helping to establish the culture sequence of south Indian prehistory</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/mandatory-palestine"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mandatory%20Palestine.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mandatory Palestine</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The UN General Assembly adopts Resolution 181 on 29 November, recommending partition into Arab and Jewish states; civil war between the two communities begins at once.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/zionism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Zionism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Zionism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The United Nations General Assembly votes to partition Palestine into separate Jewish and Arab states</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/nationalism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Nationalism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Nationalism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Against Gandhi’s composite nationalism, the Indian subcontinent is partitioned along religious lines into Pakistan and India</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/socialism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Socialism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Socialism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Britain nationalises its coal mines under Clement Attlee’s Labour government, creating a coal board to run the industry</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/imperialism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Imperialism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Imperialism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">India becomes independent, with partition, as decolonisation movements arise across the British Empire</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/free-state-of-prussia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Free%20State%20of%20Prussia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Free State of Prussia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Control Council Law No. 46 of 25 February decrees the dissolution of Prussia</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-romania"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Romania.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Romania</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">King Michael I abdicates and parliament proclaims the Romanian People's Republic</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/francoist-spain"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Francoist%20Spain.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Francoist Spain</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Spain is declared a kingdom on 26 July, with Franco as regent for life and the sole right to appoint his successor</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/jawaharlal-nehru"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Jawaharlal%20Nehru.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Jawaharlal Nehru</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">He becomes the first prime minister of independent India and gives the &quot;Tryst with Destiny&quot; speech</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/delhi"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Delhi.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Delhi</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">New Delhi becomes the capital of independent India</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/lahore"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Lahore.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Lahore</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Riots in the weeks of Partition end with Lahore awarded to Pakistan on 17 August</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/kolkata"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kolkata.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kolkata</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The partition of India and of Bengal sends hundreds of thousands of Hindus into the city</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/b-r-ambedkar"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/B.%20R.%20Ambedkar.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>B. R. Ambedkar</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Becomes Law Minister in Nehru's cabinet and is appointed Chairman of the Drafting Committee of the Constitution</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/quakers"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Quakers.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Quakers</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The British Friends Service Council and the American Friends Service Committee are awarded the Nobel Peace Prize</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/neoliberalism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Neoliberalism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Neoliberalism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Mont Pelerin Society is founded, with Hayek, Friedman, Popper, Stigler and Mises among its founding members</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/secularism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Secularism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Secularism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">India becomes a secular state on achieving independence</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/baathism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Ba'athism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Ba'athism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The first party congress meets, the two Ba'ath movements merge, and the party adopts its charter</span></li></ul></section>
